From 7828168cc7e39f44b3057f820cb5c678fe08abc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 11:57:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix missing <cstdint> include in WDBCTableReader.h

uint32_t is used throughout this header (member fields, a return type,
casts) but only <type_traits>/<fstream>/<vector>/<map>/<sstream> etc.
are included, none of which reliably pulls in <cstdint> transitively
under GCC/libstdc++ (e.g. GCC 13 on Linux). Fails with:

  error: 'uint32_t' does not name a type

which then cascades into unrelated-looking errors further down the
same header (e.g. "has no member named 'Insert'", "expected ')'
before 'fieldCount'") once the malformed declarations this produces
get used later in the file -- all from the same missing include.
---
 include/readers/wdbc/WDBCTableReader.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/include/readers/wdbc/WDBCTableReader.h b/include/readers/wdbc/WDBCTableReader.h
index 418f875..24a9926 100644
--- a/include/readers/wdbc/WDBCTableReader.h
+++ b/include/readers/wdbc/WDBCTableReader.h
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 #pragma once
+#include <cstdint>
 #include <type_traits>
 #include <fstream>
 #include <istream>
-- 
